RF.put("questb:b70",{"8630":{"id":8630,"t":"Avenger's Pauldrons","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Gold Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Life Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nAvenger's Pauldrons\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Alliance Class Paladin Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8630\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Avenger's Pauldrons this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Gold Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8790":{"id":8790,"t":"Imperial Qiraji Regalia","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Merithra of the Dream in the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj will create Elementium Infused Armaments for you should you bring her Imperial Qiraji Regalia and 3 Elementium Ore.\nImperial Qiraji Regalia\n3 Elementium Ore Blackwing Technician 7.7 % in Blackwing Lair","desc":"Arygos theorizes that the element which is born of conflicts between the Old Gods and their minions is also extremely deadly to them under the right conditions. I speak of Elementium, mortal.\nFind and bring me Imperial Qiraji Regalia and the toxic element and I shall infuse weapons of great power.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlessed Qiraji Acolyte Staff Blessed Qiraji Augur Staff Blessed Qiraji War Hammer\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You will strike them down and free us of these bonds.","done":"Use the item well, ‹name›. Let them feel the pain that they so dearly wish to inflict upon others.\nUn'Goro Crater Open the zone on the world map Start Merithra of the Dream Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Merithra of the Dream Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8790","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8710":{"id":8710,"t":"Kris of Unspoken Names","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ornate Hilt, 2 Onyx Idols, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ornate Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Onyx Idol Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Sandstalker 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nKris of Unspoken Names\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8550":{"id":8550,"t":"The Horde Needs Peacebloom!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from The Horde Needs Peacebloom!.","obj":"Bring 20 Peacebloom to Herbalist Proudfeather at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Peacebloom Peacebloom , Peacebloom , Rejold Barleybrew 50 % , Takar the Seer 40 % and 4 more","desc":"Hello again, Abyssmal. I am glad that you wish to speak to me once more concerning our neverending need for peacebloom. The war effort continues, and with it our production of potions and elixirs to aid in the battles to come. Will you help us again, ‹class›? I am in need of the same amount of peacebloom as before, so if you can gather it up and return it to me here I would be most grateful. Of course, if you already have it on your person, I will be more than happy to accept it from you now","rew":"You will receive:\nHorde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"Thank you for your continued efforts, ‹name›. You bring great honor to yourself and your ancestors with your selfless giving, and it will be known to all! I will store these herbs away so that they stay fresh until they are needed. Once again you reveal the truest spirit of the Horde, the struggle to overcome and the promise that we can work together to do so.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":33.1,"y":70.4,"n":"Herbalist Proudfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8390":{"id":8390,"t":"Conquering Arathi Basin","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Our conflict with the Alliance has escalated to a true war. No longer are false pretenses to enter into battle used or expected by either side at this point.\nThe battle for the Arathi Basin is one of resources, plain and simple. Either the Alliance gets the resources and uses them against us or we get them and use them to keep our war efforts going. Help the Defilers maintain the flow of resources we need, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with The Defilers","back":"You've come back with news from Arathi, ‹class›?","done":"Securing our resources in Arathi is an important task! You've done well, ‹name›.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1030":{"id":1030,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":28,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find an uncorrupted furbolg, and using the power of Dartol's Rod of Transformation, speak to him.\nProvided: Dartol's Rod of Transformation","desc":"Alas, I'm not completely certain what he had in mind next.\nIf what he said was true about the rod's power, then it will allow you to take on another form altogether. Which form, I do not know.\nPerhaps he meant to use its powers to get closer to the tainted furbolgs, but even the uncorrupted creatures would slaughter him were he not careful. Transformed by the rod, Dartol would have to speak to a furbolg who was safe from the effects of Fel Moss.\nI would start your search southeast of Mystral Lake.","rew":"Experience: 1,700\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Yes, yes... you are one of my kind, but still whole. Still clean.\nI am unsure how you have escaped the atrocities the night elves have visited upon our people, but I am glad to know that I am no longer alone.\nCorruption now runs through the veins of our kin, young one, corruption brought down upon us by the prideful night elves. They are the ones who did this to our people... They are the ones I blame for being cast out of my tribe.\nAt night I can still see the campfires burning in the darkness.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":50.8,"y":75.1,"n":"Krolg","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3510":{"id":3510,"t":"The Name of the Beast","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Hetaera and bring back Hetaera's Bloodied Head, Hetaera's Beaten Head, and Hetaera's Bruised Head to Lord Arkkoroc.\nHetaera's Beaten Head Hetaera\nHetaera's Bloodied Head Hetaera\nHetaera's Bruised Head Hetaera","desc":"She kills my children, mortal. She that calls herself the ruler of these oceans. A false god, nothing more. Crush her and bring back all of her heads.\nFor that, you will be given the name that you seek and something else of equal importance.\nShe roams the clutch... Hetaera she is called.\n<Lord Arkkoroc points to the southwest.>\nGo!","rew":"Money: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200","back":"<Lord Arkkoroc bends down to inspect you.>\nWhere are they?","done":"Finally, one worthy of the wisdom of Arkkoroc!","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":77.1,"y":42.8,"n":"Lord Arkkoroc","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"710":{"id":710,"t":"Study of the Elements: Rock","lv":37,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find 10 Small Stone Shards and bring them to Lotwil Veriatus in the Badlands.\n10 Small Stone Shard Lesser Rock Elemental 40 %","desc":"Here in the Badlands I've stopped to work on my latest project: my shackles of elemental binding.\nWhen complete, they will allow mages to summon even more powerful elementals for use in even greater capacities. To start things off, I need small stone shards to test some of my newest offensive spells along with a few gizmos I've pieced together.\nThe shards are easily collected from the lesser rock elementals to the west of here. Could you bring me some?","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"This area's perfect for-- Could you hold these in place for a moment? Yes, just like that, along the vector normal. Now, what was I... Right. Perfect for testing my latest project. The raw materials, the open space... what more could an intelligent and enlightened practitioner of the arts ask for?","done":"These shall do nicely, ‹name›. Thank you. Hmm, a bit more sand than I'd anticipated. Have to adjust the coefficient of friction. No, wait; it should still be negligible with the frost oil.\n<Mumbling to himself, Lotwil puts one fist into the palm of his other hand and stares at them as if fascinated.>","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"96630":{"id":96630,"t":"The adventurer","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the journal to Lyreena Duskblade near Dolanaar.\nProvided: Lost Journal","desc":"<The journal appears to be quite plain, detailing the life and adventures of someone you've never heard of.\nThere are multiple entries mentioning camping. It seems to be quite... fun.>","back":"Are you here to learn about camping in the wilderness?","done":"Is that my journal? I've been missing this for a while. Thank you, ‹class›.\nHey, you've got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.1,"y":39.5,"n":"Lost Journal","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94310":{"id":94310,"t":"Craftsmans writ black mageweave vest","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Black Mageweave Vest\nBlack Mageweave Vest","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Black Mageweave Vest, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Black Mageweave Vest Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94310","cats":["crafting"]},"94230":{"id":94230,"t":"Craftsmans writ explosive sheep","min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Explosive Sheep\nExplosive Sheep","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Explosive Sheep, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"<The distraught woman peers into the nearby farmstead. She notices you approach a moment before it might have startled her.>\nPlease tell me you are delivering one of my crafting orders!","done":"The Explosive Sheep? It's a bit smaller than I had hoped but...\n<She reached out to claim it, but then cautiously took it out from your arms. It did not take long before she delicately placed it down.>\nI'm hoping this does enough damage to scare a few off...","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":34,"y":23.3,"n":"Alyce","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"950":{"id":950,"t":"Return to Onu","lv":17,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Onu the recovered Insane Scribbles.\nInsane Scribbles\nProvided: Insane Scribbles","desc":"Peering into the Twilight Tome is maddening. Text begins to swim and dance after only a moment's glance, and once beautiful scrollwork twists into grotesque shapes.\nTearing away one page of insane scribbles is all that is possible before a swoon overtakes you.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 950\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›. You return.","done":"A chaotic, primal magic surrounds this parchment of scribbles. I sense the work of the old ones in it.\nLet us hope it reveals the purpose of the Twilight's Hammer in Darkshore...","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.5,"y":86.1,"n":"Twilight Tome","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.3,"n":"Onu","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"8950":{"id":8950,"t":"The Instigator's Enchantment","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the following to Falrin Treeshaper inside Dire Maul: 1 Jeering Spectre's Essence, 4 Dark Runes and 8 Large Brilliant Shards.\nJeering Spectre's Essence Eldreth Phantasm 20 % , Eldreth Spectre 20 % , Eldreth Spirit 20 % , Eldreth Apparition 20 % and 2 more\n4 Dark Rune Lady Illucia Barov 51.4 % in Scholomance , Instructor Malicia 44 % in Scholomance , The Ravenian 44 % in Scholomance , Lorekeeper Polkelt 44 % in Scholomance and 2 more\n8 Large Brilliant Shard","desc":"I can place the enchantment you require on the banner quite easily, ‹name›. Unfortunately I don't have the materials I need as it is very rarely that someone asks for this sort of charm.\nI will require the essence of one of the Eldreth ghosts that haunt these halls, a handful of Scholomance dark runes and some large brilliant shards. Bring me these reagents and I shall perform this task for you.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you gathered the materials I require, ‹name›?","done":"Yes, these will do just fine. After I'm done, no force in the world will be able to stop your victim from accepting your challenge.\nSilverpine Forest Open the zone on the world map Start Falrin Treeshaper End Falrin Treeshaper Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 8950\nThe chain\n40 quests at level 60, 166,950 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] In Search of Anthion\nUse the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer at the entrance to Stratholme and speak with the ghost of Anthion Harmon.\nDeliana Dun Morogh\n6,600 XP\n[ 60 ] In Search of Anthion\nUse the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer at the entrance to Stratholme and speak with the ghost of Anthion Harmon.\nMokvar Orgrimmar\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Dead Man's Plea\nGo into Stratholme and rescue Ysida Harmon from Baron Rivendare.\nAnthion Harmon Eastern Plaguelands\n8,300 XP\n3 [ 60 ] Proof of Life\nBring Ysida's Locket to Anthion Harmon in Eastern Plaguelands.\nYsida Harmon\n6,600 XP\n4 [ 60 ] Anthion's Strange Request\nBring 3 Dark Iron Bars, 20 Enchanted Leather, 3 Mooncloth and 4 Cured Rugged Hides to Anthion Harmon in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nAnthion Harmon Eastern Plaguelands\n6,600 XP\n5 [ 60 ] Anthion's Old Friend\nTake the incomplete Banner of Provocation to Falrin Treeshaper at the library in Dire Maul.\nAnthion Harmon Eastern Plaguelands\n6,600 XP\n6 [ 60 ] Falrin's Vendetta\nCollect 25 Ogre Warbeads from Ogres inside Dire Maul or Blackrock Spire and return to Falrin Treeshaper inside the Athenaeum in Dire Maul.\nFalrin Treeshaper\n6,600 XP\n7 [ 60 ] The Instigator's Enchantment this quest\nBring the following to Falrin Treeshaper inside Dire Maul: 1 Jeering Spectre's Essence, 4 Dark Runes and 8 Large Brilliant Shards.\nFalrin Treeshaper\n6,600 XP\n8 [ 60 ] The Challenge\nTravel to the Ring of the Law in Blackrock Depths and place the Banner of Provocation in its center as you are sentenced by High Justice Grimstone.\nFalrin Treeshaper\n6,600 XP\n9 [ 60 ] One quest for each class\nDruid , Hunter , Mage , Paladin , Priest , Rogue , Shaman , Warlock , Warrior , Druid , Hunter , Mage , Priest , Rogue , Warlock , Warrior\nAnthion Harmon Eastern Plaguelands\n9,950 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"310":{"id":310,"t":"Bitter Rivals","lv":6,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"In the basement of the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos, replace a barrel of Thunder Ale with a Barrel of Barleybrew Scalder.\nBarrel of Barleybrew Scalder\nProvided: Barrel of Barleybrew Scalder","desc":"I have to admit, those Thunderbrews make some good drinks. But they need to learn that theirs isn't the only decent brew! Maybe you can help me teach them that lesson...\nHere, take this barrel of Barleybrew Scalder. Sneak into the basement of the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos and switch it with one of their barrels of Thunder Ale. Then we'll see how their patrons like my brew over theirs!\nAnd if the barrels are guarded, then you might have to distract the guard ...","rew":"Experience: 140\n+25 reputation with Ironforge\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"The date on this barrel shows that it'll soon be tapped.","done":"You quickly place Marleth's barrel of Barleybrew Scalder among the Thunderbrew barrels.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.5,"n":"Marleth Barleybrew","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.7,"y":52.7,"n":"Unguarded Thunder Ale Barrel","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96390":{"id":96390,"t":"Nip em in the bud","lv":13,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 10 Dark Iron Spies in Dun Morogh.\nDark Iron Spy slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Dark Iron spies have infiltrated Dun Morogh. To what end I canna' not sure, but this is a problem we need to nip in the bud before it is allowed to grow.\nHead eastward to Ironband's Compound and kill the Dark Iron spies that you find there.","done":"These Dark Irons may be our cousins but they ain't family, that's for sure. I shed no tears for any misfortune that befalls them that stray too far from that accursed mountain o' theirs.\nHopefully this is enough to put 'em off of further incursions into these lands.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":64.8,"y":58.4,"n":"Earthseer Farsen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"790":{"id":790,"t":"Sarkoth","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Sarkoth and bring his claw back to Hana'zua.\nSarkoth's Mangled Claw Sarkoth","desc":"‹class›! I thought I would die out here with none to know of it. While I was hunting the scorpids of the Valley, I came across a particularly vicious-looking one. Hurling myself at it, I managed to inflict a massive blow to its claw before it closed around my leg.\nI wasn't ready for its stinger though, and it sliced down and into my chest, cutting into my flesh and letting my blood. Please, you must kill the scorpid for me! My honor must be upheld! I fought it up on the plateau to the south.","rew":"Experience: 450\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Ahhh... my father always said I would never amount to much, and here, lying beneath a tree as life seeps away, I'm afraid it looks like he was right.\nAt least I wish to die knowing that my last enemy in life lays dead.","done":"My blow was not enough to kill him, but looking at the damage I inflicted gives me some small measure of pride. That small measure will be all I have to sustain myself if I die, and in that light, the short list of my life's accomplishments fills me with anger.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":40.6,"y":62.6,"n":"Hana'zua","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"230":{"id":230,"t":"Sven's Camp","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Book from Sven's Farm to Sven.\nBook from Sven's Farm\nProvided: Book from Sven's Farm","desc":"Digging through the mound, you find a small, dirt-stained book.\nThe book has no title, but...it has information Sven would like to know.","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You found what?? Please, let me see it...","done":"<Sven reads the book's pages, then slams it shut.>\nThat shadowy figure I saw was a witness to my family's death! There are questions I'd like to ask that man...if only I knew who he was!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":49.9,"y":77.7,"n":"Mound of loose dirt","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"70":{"id":70,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Stalvan's Undelivered Letter from the chest and deliver it to the Canal District in Stormwind.\nAn Undelivered Letter Storage Chest , Gizmorium Shipping Crate","desc":"The name Stalvan rings a bell. I remember now.\nMany years back, on a stormy night, a messenger came in, seeking refuge for the night. Near the stroke of midnight, the man ran down the stairs screaming, his face pale with fear. Still wearing his bedclothes, he disappeared into the downpour.\nIn his haste he forgot his letters in the chest upstairs. He never returned for them. One remains from that Stalvan fellow, intended for the Canal District in Stormwind. Help yourself to it.","rew":"Experience: 1,700\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What have ya got there? Let me take a look at that. . .","done":"You've got some nerve bringing this here.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.8,"y":65.8,"n":"Innkeeper Farley","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":42.5,"y":72.4,"n":"Caretaker Folsom","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1270":{"id":1270,"t":"Stinky's Escape","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort \"Stinky\" Ignatz, then speak with Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.","desc":"Great, finally something that doesn't want to eat me!!\nI need help handling the critters around here, and you fit the mold, buddy/lady.\nA goblin from Ratchet named Mebok Mizzyrix needs some bogbean leaves for a potion, or something... I honestly don't care why -- his money was good and I know this swamp, so here I am.\nToo bad I got myself surrounded before I found the bogbean! Can you help me out of here, and watch my back as I look for Mebok's plant?","rew":"You will receive:\nElixir of Lesser Fortitude\nMoney: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","done":"Stinky was here with the herbs I ask of him, and he told me you helped him out of a bind. Good work! A friend of Stinky's is a friend of mine!\nHe asked me to give you this if I ever saw you, right before he walked back south toward the marsh.\nDustwallow Marsh The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.9,"y":17.5,"n":"\"Stinky\" Ignatz","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":37.6,"n":"Mebok Mizzyrix","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5510":{"id":5510,"t":"Minion's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Minion's Scourgestone Skeletal Terror 50 % , Slavering Ghoul 50 % , Hungering Wraith 50 % , Foulmane 50 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"A Minion's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge rank and file. These are sometimes found on the weaker of their troops positioned in the Plaguelands, though the term \"weaker\" is certainly to be considered in context. The Scourge, no matter where they are, should never be underestimated.\nThe Argent Dawn currently offers a valor token in exchange for twenty of these insignia - an exchange I'm happy to do, provided you have earned enough scourgestones!","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nThe tokens serve two purposes. One - they can be used to further your standing within the Argent Dawn; to do so may avail you options and rewards that are reserved for our honored and revered allies. Two - they can be given to our quartermasters, along with coin, as payment for some of the Dawn's more prized items.\nWhatever you decide, know that you are earning your commission. Well done!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9190":{"id":9190,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Boots","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 8 Runecloth Boots and the Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Boots - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Runecloth Boots\n8 Runecloth Boots\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Runecloth Boots","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order TR-635:\n8 Runecloth Boots.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"By Bronzebeard's beard! You actually brought me runecloth boots... I guess I lost that bet.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"8470":{"id":8470,"t":"Deadwood Ritual Totem","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Deadwood Ritual Totem inside Timbermaw Hold and see if one of the furbolgs there will find a use for the item. The Timbermaw will not speak with you unless you are of Neutral reputation or greater with them.\nDeadwood Ritual Totem Deadwood Avenger 3.3 % , Deadwood Den Watcher 3.2 % , Deadwood Shaman 3.2 %\nReach 0 reputation with Timbermaw Hold\nProvided: Deadwood Ritual Totem","desc":"You have found one of the Deadwood furbolg's ritual totems. The totem itself is of non-descript construction, but a palpable sense of despair emanates from it. If there were any object that might best exemplify the corruption that the Deadwood furbolg suffer under, this item would clearly be it.\nOne of the furbolgs inside Timbermaw Hold may have a use for such an item... that is, if you've earned their trust enough for them to speak with you.","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Major Healing Potion 2 Major Mana Potion\nMoney: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+150 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"Yes ‹class›, what can I assist you with? You walk among us peacefully, though there is assuredly something amiss. I sense something... something troubling...","done":"This totem... I recognize it as one of the Deadwood's, but it is thick with the stench of decay. Whatever foulness has turned our brethren against us is surely present in this object.\nYou were wise to bring this to us, ‹name›. Perhaps through study and ritual, we can uncover what it is that pollutes the minds of our brethren. Thank you, friend please accept these offerings in exchange for your find.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":65.5,"y":3.5,"n":"Kernda","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2870":{"id":2870,"t":"Against Lord Shalzaru","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Eliminate Lord Shalzaru, and then bring the Mysterious Relic he uncovered to Latronicus Moonspear in Feathermoon Stronghold.\nMysterious Relic Lord Shalzaru","desc":"‹name›, new scouting reports have given us a good idea on the naga chain of command. Royalty is present amongst their rank and file, and they're the ones calling all the shots.\nSpecifically, we've identified one of the crueler royals as Lord Shalzaru. Scouts report that he himself has uncovered an odd relic during a recent naga excavation in a cave south of the main ruins, across the water on the Isle of Dread.\nPut a stop to it by putting a stop to him, and bring me his relic so we can study it.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,900\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Bringing down Lord Shalzaru would certainly set their plans back weeks, if not months. On top of that, the relic he uncovered is of definite interest to us.\nHave you performed the mission given to you, ‹name›?","done":"Well played, ‹name›! Lord Shalzaru's demise will throw the naga into disarray for some time, if not permanently. The threat they pose is now under more of our control than it has ever been, and we have you to thank for it.\nHere is more bounty money from the stronghold treasury - you've earned every copper. You and yours are welcome in Feathermoon Stronghold anytime, my friend.\nOne more thing before you depart, ‹name›... if you could...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Latronicus Moonspear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"550":{"id":550,"t":"Battle of Hillsbrad","lv":32,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Darthalia's Sealed Commendation to Varimathras in the Undercity.\nDarthalia's Sealed Commendation\nProvided: Darthalia's Sealed Commendation","desc":"Because you fought with such valor and perseverance in the Battle of Hillsbrad, I have written this commendation, extolling your heroics in combat for the high command to recognize.\nTake this sealed commendation to Varimathras in the Undercity. Go with pride, ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSacred Burial Trousers Deadskull Shield Runic Darkblade\nYou will also receive:\nBand of the Undercity\nExperience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"What brings a ‹class› all the way to the Undercity from the battlefield?","done":"So you are the infamous ‹class› who struck such a decisive blow against the Alliance forces in the Hillsbrad Foothills? Word of your glorious exploits traveled quickly to the Undercity.\nYou have quite a future in the Dark Lady's ranks if you continue to show such leadership and expertise in battle.\nWhile our primary threat is the Lich King's Scourge army descending from the north, the human \"problem\" continues to impede our battle plans. You, however, have shown that the humans can and will fall.\nHillsbrad Foothills Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6070":{"id":6070,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Thotar at Razor Hill.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Thotar at Razor Hill. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time for you to begin your training.\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":68,"y":17.8,"n":"Sian'dur","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9270":{"id":9270,"t":"Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 14,300, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris wants you to take Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian to Stratholme and use it on Consecrated Earth. Defeat the entity that is exorcised from the staff and return to him.\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nAtiesh Cleansed\nProvided: Atiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian","desc":"This final task will be the most difficult of all, ‹name›. You have faced and defeated both an Old God and the Lich King's General, but now you must face the hand of Sargeras.\nTake the staff to Stratholme. It is there that you will find a piece of consecrated earth: ground where the greatest knights of Lordaeron were murdered. Place the befouled staff upon the holy ground and prepare for an entity of immense power to break from within... Defeat the demonic being that controls the staff and return to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nAtiesh, Greatstaff of the Guardian\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"8870":{"id":8870,"t":"The Lunar Festival","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to the Lunar Festival Harbinger in the Mystic Ward of Ironforge. You can also talk to Lunar Festival Harbingers in other capital cities.","desc":"It's that time of the year, ‹name›! The Cenarion Circle invites all denizens of Azeroth to partake in our celebration of the Lunar Festival. You will find the Lunar Festival Harbinger in this very city at a location marked by a blessed circle of moonlight. She can tell you more about the holiday.","done":"Welcome, ‹name›. Are you here to join in the festivities?\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Darnassus Tirisfal Glades Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.1,"y":64.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.9,"y":24,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":31.2,"y":12.5,"n":"Lunar Festival Emissary","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":72.7,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":41.7,"y":32,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":28.2,"n":"Lunar Festival Harbinger","e":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9110":{"id":9110,"t":"Plagueheart Bindings","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Bindings if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Bindings, 6 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 1 Arcane Crystal and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Bindings Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\nNexus Crystal","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Bindings\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Bindings.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"95350":{"id":95350,"t":"Welcome to azeroth","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to Orgrimmar and speak with Thrall in the Valley of Wisdom.","desc":"Its a big world down here, and our new allies are the key to our survival.\nThe Earthen Ring is a member of the \"Horde\", a proud collection of like-minded peoples. The nearby city of Thunder Bluff is a part of the horde, and further to the east lies the capital of Orgrimmar.\nSeek out the flight master in the center of Thunder Bluff. They will fly you to Orgrimmar where you will make contact with the horde warchief--Thrall, on behalf of the Windshapers. Winds guide you, ‹name›.","done":"Lok-tar, ‹class›. I am Thrall, Warchief of the Horde.\nAn Earthen Ring messenger told me to expect an emissary from the Windshapers, and here you are. I'd not have expected to see a high elf standing before me here in Orgrimmar, but the horde will welcome you as our guest all the same.\nYou have my blessing to travel through horde lands. Go with honor, Windshaper.\nMulgore Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22.4,"n":"Alaana Stormwalker","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":32,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"2950":{"id":2950,"t":"Nogg's Ring Redo","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -30s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring the Brilliant Gold Ring, a Silver Bar, a Moss Agate, and 30 silver coins to Nogg in Orgrimmar.\nBrilliant Gold Ring\nSilver Bar Tattered Chest 9 % , Battered Chest 9 % , Tattered Chest 3 % , Battered Chest 0 % and 4 more\nMoss Agate Tink Sprocketwhistle 25 % , Greater Healing Ward 11.1 % , Tattered Chest 5 % , Venture Co. Drone 4.3 % and 4 more\nProvided: Brilliant Gold Ring","desc":"No, no, no - I'm not all of the sudden saying that the ring is mine. I normally don't do this, but your information about the Dark Irons was very useful. I'll improve your ring for you, better than whomever made this simple little thing could have ever done. Probably some gnome...\nIf you bring me a bar of silver, a moss agate, and thirty silver coins for my trouble, I'll add a silver and agate lattice to the ring that will strengthen the magic inside of it. Interested?","rew":"You will receive:\nNogg's Gold Ring\nExperience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Do you have the materials I need? I can't improve on this design without everything I asked for.","done":"Here's your ring, better than before. Thanks again for the information about those Dark Iron dwarves. This seems like a reasonable lead as to how those gnomes suddenly were struck with goblin-like inspiration.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":76,"y":25.4,"n":"Nogg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7670":{"id":7670,"t":"Lord grayson shadowbreaker","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District.","desc":"The time has come, ‹name›, for you to learn about what it will take for you to acquire something you have no doubt waited on for some time... your charger.\nSpeak with Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker in Stormwind's Cathedral District. It is he who will guide you not only though the legerdemain of a Paladin's most trusted mount, but the tasks before you to acquire one of your own.\nI wish you the best in this trial. For the Light, noble <brother/sister>!","done":"I am glad to see you ‹name›. I know that you have awaited word as to how to acquire your charger, and now that time has come.\nYou will be surely tested in many different ways, but most importantly in your willingness to rise above numerous obstacles thrust before you. These are not done as a learning exercise - your stature is beyond simple educational tests. You must save your future companion from the clutches of the evil you have spent your life fighting.\nTake heed, your time has come!\nIronforge Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":23.4,"y":6.2,"n":"Brandur Ironhammer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.2,"y":33,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"3110":{"id":3110,"t":"Hallowed Rune","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Hallowed Rune and speak to Branstock Khalder in Anvilmar.\nHallowed Rune\nProvided: Hallowed Rune","desc":"While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the priest trainer Branstock. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Ach! Ya made it, ‹name›! Wonderful!\nI was gonna say, I was about to lose faith that ye'd arrive at all... get it, lose faith? It's a joke, lass... aww, nevermind. Ya didn't come here for me bad jokes anyway.","done":"I'm the one who can train ya as you start to find your way around Coldridge Valley. When ya feel yer ready, come back to me and we'll see about maybe teaching you a new spell or two to fend off the valley from them blasted troggs.\nYa got the Light on yer side, along with all of Ironforge, ‹name›... no pressure on ya to become somethin' special.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.6,"y":66.4,"n":"Branstock Khalder","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"150":{"id":150,"t":"Murloc Poachers","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Murloc Fins to Dockmaster Baren in Lakeshire.\n8 Murloc Fin Murloc Minor Oracle 76.7 % , Murloc Warrior 55 % , Murloc Tidehunter 50.9 % , Murloc Oracle 43 % and 4 more","desc":"Murlocs are becoming a problem. Larger groups of the fishmen are dropping anchor along the shores of Lake Everstill and fishing up a storm! We need them gone before they eat all the fish in the lake!\nHunt murlocs! Bring me eight of their fins and I might have something for you...","rew":"You will receive:\nDwarven Fishing Pole\nExperience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Do you have those fins? Hurry, we need those murlocs driven from the lake!","done":"Well done, ‹name›. I hope you didn't have too much trouble with those murlocs.\nIt's strange seeing them so far from the sea. I wonder if they're here because they're running from something...","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":22.6,"y":47.4,"n":"Dockmaster Baren","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8150":{"id":8150,"t":"Honoring a Hero","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Grom's Monument in the Demon Fall Canyon of Ashenvale and use Grom's Tribute at the base of the monument. Return to Javnir Nashak outside Orgrimmar before the Harvest Festival is over.\nProvided: Grom's Tribute","desc":"During the Harvest Festival of Azeroth, we give thanks to heroes for the sacrifices - in some cases ultimate sacrifices - they have given on our behalf. The Horde acknowledges many heroes, but none exemplify strength and sacrifice more than Grom Hellscream.\nHelp us honor Grom by taking this offering to his monument in the Demon Fall Canyon of Ashenvale. Place it at the base, and then return to me. I'll only be here through the end of the festival, so waste no time in giving Grom his tribute.","rew":"You will receive:\nThe Horde's Hellscream\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Horde","back":"Have you made the journey to Grom's Monument and placed his tribute there?\nThe site where the monument is still touched by the taint of the Burning Legion. Should you be less experienced in the ways of adventuring, be on your toes when approaching the monument.","done":"Grom's full name - Grommash - means \"The Giant's Heart\"; it took that and more to stand alone against Mannoroth. I think the Warchief said it best when the curse of the orcs began and ended with Grom. Fitting that Grom's sacrifice - and perhaps redemption - would be the wellspring from which the Horde flows today.\nThank you, ‹name›. You've paid tribute to a great hero today, honoring his spirit and the spirit of the Harvest Festival.\nDurotar Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":46.1,"y":13.8,"n":"Javnir Nashak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8310":{"id":8310,"t":"Breaking the Code","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 2g 70s instead of 1g 80s.","obj":"Frankal Stonebridge at Bronzebeard's Encampment in Silithus wants you to recover a Hive'Zora Silithid Brain, Hive'Ashi Silithid Brain, and a Hive'Regal Silithid Brain. Return to Frankal when you have completed this task.\nHive'Ashi Silithid Brain Hive'Ashi Stinger 20 % , Hive'Ashi Worker 20 % , Hive'Ashi Defender 20 % , Hive'Ashi Sandstalker 20 % and 3 more\nHive'Zora Silithid Brain Hive'Zora Waywatcher 20 % , Hive'Zora Tunneler 20 % , Hive'Zora Wasp 20 % , Hive'Zora Reaver 20 % and 1 more\nHive'Regal Silithid Brain Hive'Regal Ambusher 20 % , Hive'Regal Burrower 20 % , Hive'Regal Spitfire 20 % , Hive'Regal Slavemaker 20 % and 1 more","desc":"I think I can formulate an elixir that will allow us to more readily decipher the glyphs and language of the silithid and Qiraji! What do I need? Glad you asked! I need brains! More specifically, a brain from each silithid type that inhabit the hives. Bring me brains and Rutgar's work might not be for naught.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Go play with the monkey, kid. I don't have time for this.","done":"Outstanding! Don't wander off too far, kid. We might need you to take on another task or two.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":40.8,"y":88.9,"n":"Frankal Stonebridge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"78150":{"id":78150,"t":"Friend of the library","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nScholarly Pendant Erudite's Amulet\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","done":"Thanks to your donations, the library is thriving.\nPlease, take this.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"630":{"id":630,"t":"Message in a Bottle","lv":51,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay King Mukla and return to Princess Poobah with the Key to free her.\nShackle Key King Mukla","desc":"‹name›, I put my faith in you and anyone you can muster to help free me. The great Skymane King Mukla is my captor. He commands the beasts of this island, and they keep me here against my will with the aid of this chain. If you can slay him and find the key to this shackle, I shall be indebted to you greatly.\nI often hear him to the southeast side of the island, but please be careful: he is not to be trifled with.","rew":"You will receive:\nPoobah's Nose Ring\nExperience: 7,350","back":"I thank my ancestors someone has come to aid me. Do you have the key that will free me?","done":"‹name›, you have saved me from a great dishonor. If it was within my power, I would offer you a place among my tribe. But for now, all I can only offer you is this token for the courage and nobility you have shown.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":38.5,"y":80.6,"n":"Princess Poobah","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8070":{"id":8070,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Confessor's Bindings","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Sash. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Sash\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Shortly after the fall of the Gurubashi, we Zandalar almost succumbed to a final defeat from evil within our own tribe. It was then that the confessors amongst us arose, preserving the tribe by banishing out those who would destroy their own kind. They not only keep us in tune with the spirits, but they also preserve the flesh.\nGo forth into Zul'Gurub and witness first hand the depravity of Hakkar and the Gurubashi. Wrest the Paragons of Power that we seek from them; success will be rewarded!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Confessor's Bindings\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"The Paragons of Power... do you have them? Only when we have them will we be able to make use of the latent power stored inside them. It will be good to turn the tables on the minions of the Blood God...","done":"Success! These will go a long way to building up our power against the rise of Hakkar. With your help, we've taken a significant step in ensuring that the Blood God will not destroy us all.\nYou've earned honor with the tribe today, ‹name›. Take this - the confessor's bindings - as a symbol of our thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"93430":{"id":93430,"t":"Taking the bait back","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Lost One Fisherman who stole Pelluk's lure, and take it back.\nLucky Lure","desc":"Now they've really done it! As if those wretches weren't already enough to deal with, one of them has stolen my lucky lure!\nI was just out fishing this morning, when one came up out of the muck, cut my line, and ran off with it. The thief is almost certainly one of the Lost Ones' own fishermen, hoping to use the lure themselves.\nWell, our supply of fish depends on that lure, so I need it back. The Lost Ones fish along the banks east of here. Find that thief, ‹race›!","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\nSwamp of Sorrows Open the zone on the world map Level 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93430","cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"1430":{"id":1430,"t":"Fresh Meat","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Monstrous Crawler Legs to Dar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\n10 Monstrous Crawler Leg Monstrous Crawler 12 %","desc":"There's a high demand for the succulent taste of crawler meat among my customers; especially the meat from the monstrous crawlers.\nIf you plan on heading to the coast, then I could easily make it worth your while to bring me back some of their legs to have transported back to Orgrimmar.\nThe coast is to the east from here, and you should have no problem finding the creatures scurrying along the beaches and under the sea.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Grilled King Crawler Legs Leather Chef's Belt\nExperience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I have a cask of wine waiting for your success, ‹name›. It's only right I taste the goods before I have it shipped back to my customers.","done":"Ah, this should be perfect. I can't wait to taste these after they are prepared perfectly over an open fire. You should take a sample of it with you on your travels. It truly is delicious.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":44.7,"y":57.2,"n":"Dar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"870":{"id":870,"t":"The Forgotten Pools","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report back to Tonga Runetotem with your findings.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"Long ago, the Barrens was a lush place, teeming with life. But war and cataclysm raged across the land, scorching it and leaving a dry husk. Such is the way of things, and it saddens my heart.\nBut within the past few years, new oases have formed in the Barrens, and life stirs. And deep down, we druids sense a power leaking its way to the surface.\nWe must find its source. Travel to the Forgotten Pools, northwest of the Crossroads. Search its waters for a source of power, then return here.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you been to the Forgotten Pools, ‹name›? Did you find anything?","done":"You found a fissure in the earth, with gases bubbling from it? Strange. This may be an answer to our questions, but we cannot yet be sure.\nBut it is a clue. And I am grateful that you found it.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.3,"y":31.9,"n":"Tonga Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"7830":{"id":7830,"t":"Avenging the Fallen","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Markhor at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to kill a Razorbeak Skylord and retrieve its Skylord Plume. Return to him once the task is complete.\nMarkhor mentioned that the Razorbeak Skylord are a rare breed that tend to occupy the wilds of the Hinterlands.\nSkylord Plume Razorbeak Skylord","desc":"The filth that calls itself Wildhammer trains gryphon to slay troll. Horrible, I know, but worry not, justice will soon be meted out.\nFor now, I want you to focus on eradicating the elder gryphons of the region. They are known as Skylords.\nSlay one and return to me with its plume.","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"The Razorbeak Skylord is a much rarer breed of gryphon: One responsible for mating and creating murderous offspring.","done":"<Markhor examines the plume.>\nI wonder how many of our hunters this beast devoured before you brought it to justice.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.2,"y":79.5,"n":"Huntsman Markhor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1110":{"id":1110,"t":"Rocket Car Parts","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 30 Rocket Car Parts to Kravel Koalbeard in the Shimmering Flats.\n30 Rocket Car Parts Rocket Car Rubble , Rocket Car Rubble , Rocket Car Rubble , Rocket Car Rubble and 2 more","desc":"Heh heh, with all the races they're running here, it's no surprise that a few mishaps happen along the way. If you look around the Shimmering Flats then you'll see evidence of past crashes -- scraps of rocket car parts are littered everywhere!\nAnd those parts are worth money to the gnomes and goblins. They're always looking for more contraptions to slap onto their cars.\nSo go out and get me parts. Bring me a heap and I'll pay you well.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500","back":"‹name›, have you been out into the Flats? Did you bring back that load of parts I wanted?","done":"Whoa, look at all that! There's some good stuff in that heap of junk. I'm sure I can pawn it off for a hefty sum.\nAnd... is that an ear I see squashed between those two sheets of metal?? Ouch! Heh, I sure wouldn't want to be that pilot!\nThanks, ‹name›. Here's your pay. And here's some advice, free of charge...\nIf you look hard enough, you can always find profit in someone else's tragedy.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"98070":{"id":98070,"t":"Stop the screeching","lv":31,"min":27,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 5 Screeching Harpies, 5 Screeching Roguefeather Harpies and 5 Screeching Windcaller Harpies.\nScreeching Harpy slain : 0/ 5\nScreeching Roguefeather slain : 0/ 5\nScreeching Windcaller slain : 0/ 5","desc":"The Screeching Canyon is home to a local band of harpies known for their ferocious nature and raiding tactics. They have ambushed the last few supply caravans that have been brave enough to traverse this place.\nI fear if something isn't done soon, there will be no caravans that will dare make the trek to Freewind Post.\nGo, slay as many of these harpies as you are able. Return to me once the deed has been done, and I will reward you well for your efforts.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":46,"y":51.4,"n":"Jandia","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1190":{"id":1190,"t":"Keeping Pace","lv":41,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Have Zamek create a diversion, then steal Rizzle's plans for Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.","desc":"The Brassbolts brothers have discovered a new building material, that's the only explanation that makes sense. Their cars have been operating faster than before, but their designs, and all the other data we've gathered from their runs is identical.\nWhat we do know, is that Rizzle Brassbolts has been focused on the plans for this new discovery almost constantly.\nZamek can create a diversion for you, so that you can steal those plans from them.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+50 reputation with Ratchet","done":"Scribbled in a hasty, hurried hand, a scroll of notes and designs for the refinement of some raw material.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":75.9,"n":"Pozzik","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.2,"y":77.4,"n":"Rizzle's Unguarded Plans","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1510":{"id":1510,"t":"News of Dogran","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Ken'zigla at the Malaka'jin.","desc":"He was stationed at Camp Taurajo, where we've been trying to weed out the quilboar. He led a few grunts to one of their camps, where he was hurt bad. The others made it back and tried to rescue him. He was in bad shape, his wounds festered, so they were afraid to move him without patching him up first.\nThey sent a message here, requesting a healing draught from the trolls at the Malaka'jin at the base of the Stonetalon Mountains. We sent someone to get it, but they haven't returned yet.","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"Another ‹race›, eh? I hope you haven't come for the other. He didn't make it. Those goblins did him in good.\nHe said he needed a healing draught, but not much else.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.9,"y":30.3,"n":"Gazrog","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":73.2,"y":95.1,"n":"Ken'zigla","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"6390":{"id":6390,"t":"A Plague Upon Thee","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Release the Plagueland Termites in the Northridge Lumber Mill, then return with the Barrel of Plagueland Termites to Mickey Levine at the Bulwark in Tirisfal Glades.\nBarrel of Plagueland Termites\nProvided: Barrel of Plagueland Termites","desc":"You look around the lumber mill for something suitable to open the barrel with. You find a crowbar that looks like it will do the trick.\nYou set your feet and pray that you'll be able to get out of the mill before the termites get to you.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650","back":"Have you done it, ‹name›? Have you released the termites in the lumber mill?\nIt was bad enough that my family lost their jobs and lives, but then to see the place where my childhood was spent taken over by those disgusting so-called holy men... pfah!!","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Here, take this coin. I'm sorry it's not more, but try to take some joy in helping destroy the Scarlet Crusade's efforts!\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":48.3,"y":32,"n":"Termite Barrel","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.3,"y":72.3,"n":"Mickey Levine","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"470":{"id":470,"t":"Digging Through the Ooze","lv":24,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"One of the oozes at Ironbeard's Tomb has Sida's bag, retrieve it and bring it back to her in Menethil Harbor.\nSida's Bag Monstrous Ooze 15 % , Black Ooze 15 % , Crimson Ooze 15 %","desc":"On my weekly visit to Ironbeard's Tomb I was attacked by dreadful, dripping oozes! Naturally, I panicked.\nI threw my bag at one, but it didn't do anything! The ooze just sucked it right up... Luckily, it did give me enough time to get away.\nThe bad news is that I really need to get the contents of my bag!\nI don't know which ooze I threw my bag at; they all looked the same! Ironbeard's Tomb is northeast of here, near Dun Modr. Thank you so much!","rew":"You will receive:\nOoze-covered Bag\nMoney: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,400\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did you find my bag?","done":"Oh, thank you, ‹name›! I was afraid that it was lost for good!\n<She quickly empties the contents of the ooze-covered bag onto the ground, before scooping them up.>\nHm, I don't have much use for this anymore, but wash it off and I'm sure you could make use of it.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.8,"y":58,"n":"Sida","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98230":{"id":98230,"t":"This land was their land","lv":29,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Howin Kindfeather east of Menethil Harbor, along the road.","desc":"After the War of the Three Hammers that tore dwarven life as we knew it apart, the Wildhammers settled here, founding the mountain fortress of Grim Batol.\nIt was a wondrous place. Gryphons soared everywhere you looked, diving down through the wetlands to grab a fish.\nIt didn't last long, sadly.\nHowin Kindfeather is one of the first Wildhammers to return in ages. Keeps to himself, far outside of town. Follow the road east--you'll find him eventually. He could surely use a hand.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.8,"y":57.4,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.4,"y":42,"n":"Howin Kindfeather","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98310":{"id":98310,"t":"Gleaning our future","lv":32,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Goaz Stone near Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru and bring their hearts back to Prospector Whelgar.\nHeart of Ados\nHeart of Modr\nHeart of Golm\nHeart of Neru","desc":"There are other, larger golems all around the Wetlands. They each bear inscriptions marking them as Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru--matching the missing pieces of the Goaz Stone you found!\nI'd be willing to bet if we can bring pieces of them as well, we'll reveal more of the Goaz Stone!\nYou'll find Ados at the Dragonmaw Gates to the east, near Grim Batol. Modr is right outside Dun Modr to the north. Golm lies beneath Grim Batol, east of Dun Algaz. Neru's behind Direforge Hill, to the northeast.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGolem War Cloak Rune-Etched Ring Giantstone Medallion\nExperience: 3,200","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.8,"y":52.2,"n":"Prospector Whelgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92470":{"id":92470,"t":"Foul matriarch","lv":5,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 8 Ursera Scavengers and collect the head of the den mother, Urs'anah in Thendal Grove.\nUrsera Scavenger slain : 0/ 8\nHead of Urs'anah","desc":"Rorian informed you that I've been watching you. I now offer you a test of resolve. However, be warned--it will send you into great danger.\nGo to the caves to the south. Thin out the ursera's numbers there, and find their matriarch, one the rangers call \"Urs'anah\". Put her down and bring me proof of her demise. Once you have done that, you will have taken an important step on your path.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWorn Greatsword Novice's Quarterstaff Scout Ranger's Dagger Peacekeeper's Pickhammer Refined Shortbow\nMoney: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"What I ask of you is not easy, but you must be prepared for much greater challenges if you are to survive long enough to be of service to Zephras Isle.","done":"Very well done. You've felled beasts and laid low cultist interlopers. You have shown great promise but your path must soon take you beyond the relative safety of Thendal Village.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Aetheen of the Gales","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92550":{"id":92550,"t":"Havoc in the highlands","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Travel to the ruins of Falaath Village and slay 6 Al'Aketh Stormcallers, 4 Living Lightning and take the head of Commander Cyclas.\nAl'Aketh Stormcaller slain : 0/ 6\nLiving Lightning slain : 0/ 4\nCommander Cyclas's Head","desc":"Our best defense here might just be a strong offense. The advantage we now have is that we expect an attack is coming. What they won't expect is for us to hit them first.\nI've already asked a lot of you, but please head back over to Falaath Village. Kill as many cultists as you can and if you can get close enough, kill the commander and bring me his head. I'll stay here and organize the citizens and our few peacekeepers to prepare a defense... just in case you don't return.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWolfhide Belt Elegant Cuffs Ex-Commander's Gauntlets\nMoney: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"It feels good to turn the tables on these zealots.","done":"Thank the winds you've returned!\nSania Silverstream snuck out of town just before you returned, no doubt fleeing at the sight of our people arming themselves.\nYou've done an incredible thing for the people of Shen'dar Village and we owe you a debt of gratitude. If the cult returns to the highlands, they will find that Shen'dar is not such an easy target.\nWinds guide you, Zaelriel.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});